/-!
# Checked chosen-natural preliminaries

The full normalizer orbit is reduced and elementary abelian. Its centralizer
is the normalizer orbit of the seed centralizer, and a nontrivial central part
forces the source Thompson commutator. Actual central-cover coordinates prove
both centralizer vanishings in the full SL₃ row and the degree bound in the
Sp₄ and G₂ rows, including nonsplit extensions.

The full central-part alternative and TI conclusion now use the completed
nonzero-fixed-space invariance theorem of 3.2.5 without an extra premise.
The exact prime-to-p residual assertions of 11.0.4(1--2) are proved for
every source prime, retaining full SL₃ and both literal quotient maps.
Homogeneity of the literal full quotient is proved in all three natural
rows, using the original Sylow-invariant seed and the actual automorphism
factorizations. H-star intersection normalization is proved in both the Sp₄
and G₂ rows, with all earlier classification and action premises discharged.
Thus every clause of 11.0.3 is available here. The even-degree SL₃ order-three
clause of 11.0.4 is proved for cubics normalizing the seed, including the case
V = V_M. The general natural-constituent containment and action-kernel transport
are also proved. A genuine doubled natural marking of V_M now supplies an
invariant constituent and proves the cubic clause even when the seed moves.
The literal full orbit now has positive finite natural multiplicity s and
binary dimension 3ns. A strict bound dim(V_M) < 9n supplies the alternative
V_M = V or a marked double and hence the original cubic conclusion. This
numerical bound remains to be proved; homogeneity alone does not discharge it.
The original component action has exact quadratic ratio one half, and the
literal LT action on the chosen quotient has cubic ratio at most one half.
Thus the D.3.9 expression 2/q-hat is at least four on this action. Three
natural copies admit a faithful hyperplane actor of rank 2n and fixed
codimension 3n, so the numerical budget alone does not prove the strict
dimension bound. This local calculation does not refute the full ambient
source theorem. The full orbit's original L/O₂(L) action now has exact
quadratic ratio s/2, with its quotient representative equations retained.
The constituent count now proves cubic containment for every multiplicity
not divisible by three, without the stronger one/two-copy restriction.
Consequently an escaping cubic on the original D and S forces positive
multiplicity 3k and dimension 9nk. The remaining ambient exclusion of these
multiplicities is still open; the conditional dimension criterion retains
that obligation with the preliminary source owner.

The full-orbit action now has kernel prime to three and its actual component
image has the original full SL₃ marking. The ambient rank bound therefore
excludes the moved order-three alternative of D.3.9(2b) and any commuting
perfect subgroup with order divisible by three. The qrc bound now selects an actual minimal cubic actor. Its component
kernel centralizes Fitting: D.2.13's four-dimensional five-core support is
excluded by the natural dimension bound, and the rank argument controls the
entire cyclic three-core through its first omega. If this kernel is nontrivial,
it moves a three-free component whose actual actor orbit is generated by
commutators with that kernel. The exact split-prime residuals and the complete
known-simple catalogue now exclude this branch when four divides the field
degree, supplying the literal faithful conjugation action of a selected actor.
Otherwise a nonfaithful actor forces degree two modulo four and a five-element
in the same moved component, with its orbit and commutator equality retained.
The full moved support of any subgroup commuting with the original SL₃
image is now proved not to be Irr⁺. For the same nonfaithful actor and
component orbit, every actor-invariant Irr⁺ constituent has restricted ratio
strictly below two: the other D.2.7 alternative would make it the whole
moved support. Theorem A and the complete A.3.6 catalogue now identify
that same component by an actual Suzuki matrix-group isomorphism. The
strict-ratio result supplies the terminal contradiction to a Suzuki
endpoint constituent while retaining its actual action. The layer five-rank
bound now proves that the original actor normalizes this component, so its
full orbit equals that same component. Odd outer order and homogeneous
selection construct an actual actor-invariant Irr⁺ constituent of that orbit.
Its literal restricted actor has ratio strictly below two. The endpoint
argument now places this actor image inside the component image and passes
it faithfully to the literal irreducible central quotient. The genuine
Chapter K hypotheses construct natural Suzuki coordinates there, giving
the lower bound two; fixed-codimension monotonicity lifts the bound to the
original constituent. This closes the nonfaithful branch for every even
field degree and supplies the literal injective conjugation action of every
starred actor. B.2.7 and B.5 now bound the full natural multiplicity by two
when L=[L,J(T)], proving cubic containment in this genuine ambient branch.
A moving H-star intersection supplies that identity. Conversely, an escaping
cubic forces J(T) to centralize the original seed; every H-star intersection
normalizes the seed and every H-star subgroup centralizes Ω₁Z(T). Excluding
this remaining configuration is still required for unconditional 11.0.4.
The full-module FF branch now also gives at most two natural copies and
cubic containment without a Thompson-commutator assumption: starred-actor
faithfulness puts the original component in the full offender subgroup.
Any escaping cubic therefore forces the full module to be non-FF with
1 < q-hat ≤ 2, and J(T) centralizes the entire V_M. The remaining qrc
analysis must exclude this configuration on the original ambient inputs.

For the 11.2.2 consumers on the original seed, the cubic lift lies in N_G(V).
The checked seed containment therefore discharges the full-automizer cubic
premise directly. SeedAutomizer supplies the fixed-codimension and root-geometry
families in all rows and connects them to the literal centralizer/residual and
global-parameter consumers. Unrestricted cubic containment in N_G(L) remains open.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript, 1 March 2004, printed p.760.
-/
